      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Experts, help me please. To solve this problem, we need to use the relationship between the least common multiple (LCM) and the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers. Specifically, for any two integers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), the product of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is equal to the product of their LCM and GCD. This can be expressed as:\n\n\\[\na \\times b = \\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b)\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- The least common multiple \\(\\text{LCM}(a, b) = 36\\)\n- The greatest common divisor \\(\\text{GCD}(a, b) = 6\\)\n\nWe need to find the product of the two numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). Using the relationship above, we substitute the given values:\n\n\\[\na \\times b = 36 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = 216\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of the two numbers is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
