      "text": "Given that the least common multiple (LCM) of two integers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 36 and their greatest common divisor (GCD) is 6, we need to determine the product of the two numbers.\n\nWe start with the relationship between the LCM and GCD of two numbers:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\nSubstituting the given values into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = a \\times b\n\\]\nCalculating the product on the left side:\n\\[\n216 = a \\times b\n\\]\nThus, the product of the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
