    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The least common multiple of two numbers is the smallest number that is a multiple of both of them. The greatest common divisor of two numbers is the largest number that divides both of them without leaving a remainder. \n\nGiven that the least common multiple of two numbers is 36 and the greatest common divisor is 6, we want to find the product of the two numbers.\n\nWe know that the product of two numbers is equal to the product of their least common multiple and their greatest common divisor. So, if we let the two numbers be \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), then the product of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is:\n\n\\[ a \\cdot b = \\text{lcm}(a, b) \\cdot \\text{gcd}(a, b) \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[ a \\cdot b = 36 \\cdot 6 \\]\n\\[ a \\cdot b = 216 \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of the two numbers is \\(\\boxed{216}\\).",
